      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T01:48:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not opposed to exposing bounds functionality in CK. However, the `filterBounds` API is likely going to change (in particular the `MapDirection` parameter and overloaded parameter meanings is problematic). I don\u0027t want to add a new API to CK that just matches an API that will be updated in the next few months.\n\nAnother thing to consider is that with this implementation in CK, `filterBounds()` is only calculating the forward bounds and always with an identity matrix. This is, integer vs. float aside, equivalent to `computeFastBounds()`. I don\u0027t know if CK exposes that on mask filters or SkPaint as an existing precedent to follow?",
      "parentUuid": "da919dbd_105cbb5e",
